{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>The people are bringing much.</b> It is difficult: is it a bad thing that the house of our Elohim should have treasuries of gold for honor and splendor? Rather, they did not come to complain about what was brought into the house of HaShem of gold and silver etc., but about what was brought already fashioned into crafted work — which is something that has no need, and moreover is subject to deterioration, once there is already sufficient supply. And this is what he said: <b>they are bringing much</b> etc. <b>beyond the service of the work</b> — meaning, they are bringing more than the measure of service required for the work that YHWH commanded. From this you learn that they were meticulous about the details of the service. And the proof for our words is the proclamation of the herald: <b>Let them not make any more work for the sacred tribute</b>, and his saying <b>And the people were restrained from bringing</b> — and it does not say 'from making,' for Scripture states a thing that was recognizable to the wise men who were engaged in the work, and that is the bringing."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:37:05.493776376Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}